    slots: [{"key":"seo.metaTitle","kind":"text","group":"SEO","label":"Page title","def":"Quebec Law 25 Compliance Guide for Businesses | Davnoot"},{"key":"seo.metaDescription","kind":"text","group":"SEO","label":"Meta description","def":"A plain-language guide to Quebec's Law 25 privacy requirements for businesses — what it covers, deadlines, and practical steps to get compliant."},{"key":"hero.badge","kind":"inline","group":"Hero","label":"hero.badge","def":"Guide · Quebec privacy law"},{"key":"hero.title","kind":"inline","group":"Hero","label":"hero.title","def":"Law 25, in<br />plain <em>language</em>."},{"key":"hero.sub","kind":"inline","group":"Hero","label":"hero.sub","def":"Law 25 (formerly Bill 64) reshaped how Quebec businesses are required to handle personal information, and a lot of the digital marketing and website practices companies have run for years now carry real compliance risk. This guide breaks down what actually matters, in plain language."},{"key":"section1.eyebrow","kind":"inline","group":"What Law 25 requires, in short","label":"section1.eyebrow","def":"What Law 25 requires, in short"},{"key":"section1.title","kind":"inline","group":"What Law 25 requires, in short","label":"section1.title","def":"What Law 25<br /><em>requires</em>."},{"key":"section1.list.0.title","kind":"inline","group":"What Law 25 requires, in short","label":"section1.list.0.title","def":"Clear, specific consent before collecting personal information"},{"key":"section1.list.0.desc","kind":"inline","group":"What Law 25 requires, in short","label":"section1.list.0.desc","def":"No more buried, vague privacy policies."},{"key":"section1.list.1.desc","kind":"inline","group":"What Law 25 requires, in short","label":"section1.list.1.desc","def":"A designated person responsible for the protection of personal information at your organization."},{"key":"section1.list.2.desc","kind":"inline","group":"What Law 25 requires, in short","label":"section1.list.2.desc","def":"Mandatory breach notification to affected individuals and Quebec's privacy regulator (the CAI)."},{"key":"section1.list.3.desc","kind":"inline","group":"What Law 25 requires, in short","label":"section1.list.3.desc","def":"The right for individuals to request deletion or portability of their personal data."},{"key":"section1.list.4.desc","kind":"inline","group":"What Law 25 requires, in short","label":"section1.list.4.desc","def":"Privacy impact assessments before adopting new technology that handles personal data."},{"key":"section2.eyebrow","kind":"inline","group":"Where this touches your marketing","label":"section2.eyebrow","def":"Where this touches your marketing"},{"key":"section2.title","kind":"inline","group":"Where this touches your marketing","label":"section2.title","def":"Where it touches<br />your <em>marketing</em>."},{"key":"section2.p0","kind":"inline","group":"Where this touches your marketing","label":"section2.p0","def":"Cookie consent banners, email opt-ins, <a href=\"/services/meta-ads\" class=\"text-link\" data-cursor>ad pixel tracking</a>, and even how your CRM stores lead data all fall under Law 25's scope. Non-compliant cookie consent setups and vague privacy policies are two of the most common gaps we see when we audit Quebec business websites."},{"key":"section3.eyebrow","kind":"inline","group":"Practical next steps","label":"section3.eyebrow","def":"Practical next steps"},{"key":"section3.title","kind":"inline","group":"Practical next steps","label":"section3.title","def":"Practical <em>next steps</em>."},{"key":"section3.p0","kind":"inline","group":"Practical next steps","label":"section3.p0","def":"Review your website's consent banner and <a href=\"/privacy\" class=\"text-link\" data-cursor>privacy policy</a> first — they're the most visible (and most commonly non-compliant) piece. Then audit what personal data your marketing stack actually collects and where it's stored, and confirm someone at your organization is formally responsible for it."},{"key":"section3.p1","kind":"inline","group":"Practical next steps","label":"section3.p1","def":"This guide is educational and not legal advice — for a formal compliance opinion, talk to a Quebec privacy lawyer. If you want your website and marketing stack reviewed for the practical gaps we see most often, that's a conversation we're glad to have."},{"key":"cta.eyebrow","kind":"inline","group":"Final CTA","label":"cta.eyebrow","def":"Quebec Law 25"},{"key":"cta.title","kind":"inline","group":"Final CTA","label":"cta.title","def":"Find the gaps<br />we see <em>most</em>."},{"key":"cta.sub","kind":"inline","group":"Final CTA","label":"cta.sub","def":"This guide is educational and not legal advice. If you want your website and marketing stack reviewed for the practical gaps we see most often, book a free 30-minute call."}],
